---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy/" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What personal data the Neurally website collects, why, who processes it, how long it is kept and what your rights are under UK GDPR."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <section class="pt-10 pb-12 lg:pt-14">
    <div class="container-page">
      <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
      <h1 class="text-display mt-10 lg:mt-14">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl">
        What this site collects, why, and what your rights are. It is a short list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section data-tone="paper" class="py-section-sm">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="prose prose-neurally">
        <p>
          Neurally is a trading name of Stuart Davis. Stuart is the data controller for personal data
          collected through this site. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form.</strong> Your name, work email, company and role (optional) and message are
            submitted through{" "}
            <a href="https://web3forms.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Web3Forms
            </a>
            , a third-party form-delivery service, and forwarded to {site.email}. Web3Forms processes this
            data under its own privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI maturity assessment.</strong> Your answers are scored in your browser and are not
            stored. Only if you choose to send your results does the same information as the contact form,
            plus your answers and score, go through Web3Forms to {site.email}. We count anonymous completions
            by result type in GoatCounter.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Booking a call.</strong> If you book via{" "}
            <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Calendly
            </a>
            , Calendly processes your name, email and chosen time under its own privacy policy. Calendly is an
            external link: nothing from Calendly loads on this site.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics.</strong> This site uses{" "}
            <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              GoatCounter
            </a>
            , a cookie-free analytics service that counts page visits in aggregate, without cookies or
            personal data.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
        <p>
          It sets no cookies and uses no advertising or tracking pixels. Fonts, images and scripts are served
          from this site itself. The only third-party requests are the GoatCounter visit count and, when you
          submit a form, the Web3Forms submission.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on{" "}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Cloudflare
          </a>
          Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data such as IP addresses in order
          to deliver pages and protect the service.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep enquiry and booking information for as long as needed to respond to you and, where a working
          relationship follows, for the ordinary course of that engagement. Then we delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR, you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data we hold about you. Email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you're unhappy with how your data has been handled, you can complain to the
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Information Commissioner's Office
          </a>
          .
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This notice may be updated as the site or the tools behind it change. Last updated November 2026.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
